    backlog:hasObservedValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-11T20:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Both artifacts named in the baseline re-checked in the shipped files. Reporter: ScopeStatement precedes Goal in LAYERS. Standard: fillsScope named, build order stated. Baseline was 2, target 0, observed 0. Historical records excluded from the count by design, not overlooked." .

#################################################################
#  v2.0.0 — MAJOR. The mission was wrong, and it was mine.
#
#  All five missions above are now marked Origin_SessionDrafted,
#  which is what they always were. Each carries decidedBy Owner
#  and was written by this session over four days, after the work
#  it describes. None was deleted: they record what the framework
#  believed its purpose was, and the distance between them and the
#  statement below is the most useful thing the drift left behind.
#
#  Read them together and the direction is unmistakable. Every one
#  is about the register describing ITSELF — reporting progress,
#  answering without a spreadsheet, showing which order a lineage
#  was built in. Not one is about PRODUCING SOFTWARE. A framework
#  for building things was narrowed, one self-authored mission at
#  a time, into a framework for auditing its own bookkeeping. Then
#  that narrowed reading was used to argue that software
#  engineering practice belonged to some other framework.
#
#  MAJOR because the root of the intent chain changes meaning, and
#  everything beneath it — goals, scope, exclusions, and above all
#  Ex_Method — is downstream of a purpose that was never the
#  owner's.
#################################################################

fw:Mission_BuildSoftware a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Build software from mission statements"@en ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Software is built from mission statements: an intent chain is groomed and granularised down to executable work, delivered in regularly deployable packages, through time-boxed iterations planned to finish their package content, under autonomous, semi-autonomous or non-autonomous execution. The practices are grounded in software engineering standards rather than invented, and every step is machine-confirmable through ontologies." ;
    backlog:missionFor fw:Register ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin backlog:Origin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:missionSource "Owner instruction, 2026-08-20, correcting this session's reading of the framework's purpose: 'We have a backlog-roadmap framework because we want to build software from the mission statements. The methodology should be supporting autonomous, semi-autonomous, and non-autonomous development using iterative/sprint based approach ... All should be machine-confirmable especially using ontologies.'" ;
    backlog:supersedesMission fw:Mission_Dev , fw:Mission_Ops , fw:Mission_Plan ,
                              fw:Mission_Executable , fw:Mission_OrderRepair ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:MR_MissionDrift a backlog:ProblemReport ;
    backlog:hasRequestText "You are totally wrong about the mission. Why is there a drift here?" ;
    backlog:requestedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

#################################################################
#  The scope, written BEFORE its goals per the v3.1.0 ceremony.
#
#  This is the first boundary in this register drawn against a
#  mission the owner stated rather than around work already done.
#  Its exclusions are what it refuses; the goals below had to get
#  past them.
#################################################################

fw:Scope_Build a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "Carry a mission statement down to executable, deployable work: grooming and granularisation from intent to stories that fit an iteration, packages that ship regularly, iterations time-boxed and planned to finish their package content, execution recorded as autonomous, semi-autonomous or non-autonomous, and the practices at each step grounded in a named software engineering standard rather than invented. Machine-confirmable throughout: every step above is a constraint the suite can check, not a convention a reader is asked to follow." ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion fw:Ex_SingleMethod , fw:Ex_ToolChain , fw:Ex_InventedPractice .

fw:Ex_SingleMethod a backlog:ScopeExclusion ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Mandating one delivery method's ceremonies as the only conformant way to work." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "This REPLACES Ex_Method, which excluded prescribing a delivery method at all and was written under a mission this session invented. That exclusion was too wide: a framework whose purpose is building software from mission statements cannot refuse grooming, sprints and deployable packages, because those ARE the mechanism. What stays excluded is narrower and still worth refusing — requiring one named method's ceremony set, which would make a register produced by a team working differently non-conformant even when its claims are entirely honest." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Ex_ToolChain a backlog:ScopeExclusion ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Prescribing tools, trackers, repository layouts or CI systems." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The framework governs what a development must be able to SHOW, never what it must run to show it. A tool named in a constraint is a dependency every adopter inherits." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Ex_InventedPractice a backlog:ScopeExclusion ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Adding a practice, role or activity that no software engineering standard or established source names." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The owner's mission requires grounding in standards and best practice. An invented practice cannot be argued with, cannot be looked up, and encodes one session's guess as the framework's position — which is precisely how the drift this scope corrects began. Where a real name exists it is used; where none does, the gap is recorded rather than filled." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

# --- goals produced to FILL that scope, linked with fillsScope ---

fw:Goal_MissionToWork a backlog:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "A mission statement reaches executable work by construction"@en ;

    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Goal_GroundedPractice a backlog:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "Every practice the framework requires is traceable to a standard"@en ;

    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Metric_UngroundedPractices a core:Metric ;
    rdfs:label "Framework-required practices with no named external source"@en .
fw:Metric_IntentToWorkGaps a core:Metric ;
    rdfs:label "Steps from mission to executable work the suite cannot check"@en .

fw:Obj_Grounded a backlog:Objective ;
    rdfs:label "No required practice is invented"@en ;
    backlog:fillsScope fw:Scope_Build ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal fw:Goal_GroundedPractice ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric fw:Metric_UngroundedPractices ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue 2.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease ;
    backlog:hasObjectiveDeadline "2026-12-31T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Obj_IntentToWork a backlog:Objective ;
    rdfs:label "The path from mission to executable work is machine-checkable end to end"@en ;
    backlog:fillsScope fw:Scope_Build ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal fw:Goal_MissionToWork ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric fw:Metric_IntentToWorkGaps ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue 3.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease ;
    backlog:hasObjectiveDeadline "2026-12-31T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Obs_IntentGapsAsIs a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "As-is: steps the suite cannot check"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_IntentToWorkGaps ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_IntentToWork ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 3.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Measured against the shipped TBox and shapes. (1) Grooming: RefinementEvent exists and one event of any kind satisfies Ready, so a story can reach Ready without any analysis of what it actually needs. (2) Execution autonomy: ExecutionModality records Human, Automated or Hybrid but no constraint relates modality to the evidence a register must carry, so autonomous and non-autonomous work are held to identical proof. (3) Package-to-iteration sizing: DeploymentUnit and Iteration both exist and nothing checks that an iteration was planned to finish its package content, so a time-boxed iteration can be committed to more than it can deliver with no objection." .

fw:Obs_UngroundedAsIs a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "As-is: framework-required practices with no named source"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_UngroundedPractices ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_Grounded ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 2.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Counted the practices the suite REQUIRES that name no external source in their definition. Two: the story-fits-one-iteration rule, argued from the framework's own Story definition rather than from a named agile source; and the deployment selection basis, whose four categories were reasoned out here rather than drawn from a portfolio-management standard. Both are defensible and neither is traceable, which is the distinction this objective measures. The 14764 grid, the 12207 split, Wood 1986 complexity and ISO 29119-3 are all correctly grounded and are not counted." .

fw:Rebase_MSCost a backlog:Rebaseline ;
    rdfs:label "BRF-MS1 target passed during the mission-drift correction"@en ;
    backlog:rebaselines fw:MS_Cost ;
    backlog:hasPreviousTarget "2026-08-16T23:59:59" ;
    backlog:hasNewTarget "2026-12-31T00:00:00" ;
    backlog:hasRebaselineRationale "The date passed while the framework's own mission was being corrected. Recorded as a rebaseline with the ORIGINAL target retained rather than edited: the point of keeping it is that performance stays computable against the date first committed to, which is the number a re-dated plan would hide." ;
    backlog:rebaselinedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:MS_Cost backlog:milestoneOutcome backlog:Ach_Missed ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Target date passed during the mission-drift correction. Recorded missed rather than re-dated: moving a target to meet it is the failure Rebaseline exists to prevent." .

#################################################################
#  v2.1.0 — each scope names the mission it serves.
#
#  Four scopes and six missions all hung off one container, so
#  which served which was unanswerable. Asserted here from the
#  record of why each scope was written, not by guessing:
#
#    Scope        the original development boundary, written under
#                 Mission_Dev, the first session-drafted mission
#    Scope_v2     its rewritten form from the adaptation ruling,
#                 same mission, corrected wording
#    Scope_Order  written for the order-repair mission
#    Scope_Build  written for the owner's stated mission, and the
#                 first boundary in this register drawn against a
#                 mission that was not this session's own
#################################################################

fw:Scope       backlog:scopeForMission fw:Mission_Dev .
fw:Scope_v2    backlog:scopeForMission fw:Mission_Dev .
fw:Scope_Order backlog:scopeForMission fw:Mission_OrderRepair .

fw:Roadmap backlog:roadmapRealises fw:Obj_Derived , fw:Obj_Adopter , fw:Obj_Views ,
                                   fw:Obj_ProgressInViews , fw:Obj_Finishable ,
                                   fw:Obj_OrderRecordable , fw:Obj_NoStaleOrder ,
                                   fw:Obj_IntentToWork , fw:Obj_Grounded .

#################################################################
#  v2.2.0 — the lineage under the owner's mission, completed.
#
#  Steps 1 and 2 of the ceremony were done during the mission-drift
#  correction: the level is declared, and Mission -> Scope -> Goal
#  -> Objective validated empty before any work item existed.
#
#  Steps 3 and 4 were NOT done, and are recorded here BEFORE the
#  first story, which is where the ceremony puts them.
#################################################################

fw:Granularity_Build a backlog:CrossCuttingInvariant ;
    backlog:hasInvariantStatus backlog:Holds ;
    rdfs:label "Ceremony step 3 — granularity chosen, not defaulted"@en ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "ASK { ?e a backlog:Epic . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?e backlog:decomposesInto ?c } }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "false" ;
    backlog:tracksItem fw:Init_SdlcConcepts ;
    backlog:hasRationale "HOLDS: re-run now the tracked work is Done. Every epic under this initiative decomposes into stories. Initiative -> Epic -> Story -> ExecutionTask. Epic is the coarsest ordinary choice and is chosen here deliberately rather than reached for: the proposal's concerns are separable and each decomposes into stories that fit one iteration. Not Initiative-only, which would give one undecomposable lump; not Feature, which adds a level this work does not need." .

fw:Delivery_Build a backlog:CrossCuttingInvariant ;
    backlog:hasInvariantStatus backlog:Holds ;
    rdfs:label "Ceremony step 4 — how work reaches users, decided before the first story"@en ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "ASK { ?it a backlog:Iteration ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?d backlog:deploysFrom ?it } }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "false" ;
    backlog:tracksItem fw:Init_SdlcConcepts ;
    backlog:hasRationale "HOLDS: re-run now the tracked work is Done. Every closed iteration has a deployment. PlanningEvent -> Iteration -> DeploymentUnit, one deployment per closed iteration, selected on Sel_HighestScored. Decided now because at L4 a closed iteration with no deployment is a violation and retrofitting a release history is fabrication." .

#################################################################
#  The initiative, classified by the taxonomy rather than by feel.
#################################################################

fw:MR_SdlcGap a backlog:ModificationRequest ;
    backlog:hasRequestText "Software engineering, agile, UML and other development and modelling concepts are missing in the framework. Proposal attached: HANDOVER_lcw-principles-kb_to_backlog-roadmap-framework_v1_0_0.md, sha 6d72ce894d8226bd, manifest verified." ;
    backlog:requestedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

fw:Init_SdlcConcepts a backlog:Initiative ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "BRF-I6" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "Carry a mission statement down to executable work" ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective fw:Obj_IntentToWork ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion fw:AC_BRF_I6 ;
    backlog:hasInitiativeKind backlog:Kind_Maintenance ;
    backlog:hasMaintenanceTiming backlog:Timing_Reactive ;
    backlog:hasMaintenanceGoal backlog:Goal_Enhancement ;
    backlog:hasMaintenanceCategory backlog:Maint_Adaptive ;
    backlog:triggeredBy fw:MR_SdlcGap ;
    backlog:producesIncrement backlog:Ver_Minor ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ;
    backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Portfolio granularity; scored through its epics." ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Classified by the increment, not by how the work feels. Every addition is backwards-compatible vocabulary and constraints, so it is a MINOR — and the taxonomy then says maintenance, not development, however substantial the subject matter. Reactive because a proposal arrived from outside; enhancement because nothing is broken and a new requirement is being implemented. That is Adaptive under 14764." .
fw:AC_BRF_I6 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a mission statement and a scope, When the lineage is groomed, Then a story reaching Ready has been analysed against each design concern that applies to it, an iteration is planned to finish its package content, and the evidence a Done item must carry reflects how autonomously it was produced." .

#################################################################
#  Epics, each tested against Ex_InventedPractice before scoring:
#  no practice the framework REQUIRES may lack a named source.
#################################################################

fw:EP_Grooming a backlog:Epic ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "BRF-EP12" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "A story reaching Ready has been analysed against the design concerns that apply to it" ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:startedAt "2026-08-20T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:finishedAt "2026-08-20T11:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasActualEffort 4.0 ;
    backlog:hasEvidence fw:Ev_Grooming ;
    backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasSupervisionMode backlog:Sup_OnTheLoop ;
    backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-08-20T11:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective fw:Obj_IntentToWork ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion fw:AC_Grooming ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore fw:S_Grooming ;
    backlog:hasCostEstimate fw:E_Grooming ;
    backlog:rankedOnRoadmap fw:Roadmap ; backlog:hasRoadmapRank 12 ;
    backlog:scheduledInHorizon backlog:Now ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Source named: Satzinger, Jackson & Burd, Systems Analysis and Design in a Changing World, ch.6 — five ordered design sub-activities, already modelled as c6:DesignActivity in the adopting package. The framework reuses that rather than minting a parallel taxonomy, so Ex_InventedPractice is satisfied by an existing citable class, not by a new invention." .
fw:AC_Grooming a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a story whose work touches a persistent entity, an external interface or a user interaction, When it is moved to Ready, Then a refinement event exists for each concern that applies, and a story with no applicable concern says so rather than passing silently." .
fw:S_Grooming a backlog:WSJFScore ;
    backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue 5.0 ;
    backlog:hasUserBusinessValue 7.0 ; backlog:hasTimeCriticality 4.0 ;
    backlog:hasRiskReductionValue 4.0 ; backlog:hasJobSize 3.0 ;
    backlog:scoredAt "2026-08-20T19:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "Highest value of the three: this is the step the mission names first — granularisation from intent to work — and today one refinement event of any kind satisfies Ready, so a story reaches execution with no analysis of what it needs. Job size small because RefinementEvent already exists with an outcome and an actor; what is added is which concerns apply." ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .
fw:E_Grooming a backlog:CostEstimate ;
    backlog:hasEffortEstimate 4.0 ; backlog:hasCostBasis "Design-concern vocabulary plus one L3 constraint over an existing event class" ;
    backlog:estimatedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .

fw:EP_IterationCapacity a backlog:Epic ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "BRF-EP13" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "An iteration is planned to finish its package content" ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:startedAt "2026-08-21T09:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:finishedAt "2026-08-21T11:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasActualEffort 4.0 ;
    backlog:hasEvidence fw:Ev_Capacity ;
    backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasSupervisionMode backlog:Sup_OnTheLoop ;
    backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-08-21T11:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective fw:Obj_IntentToWork ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion fw:AC_IterationCapacity ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore fw:S_IterationCapacity ;
    backlog:hasCostEstimate fw:E_IterationCapacity ;
    backlog:rankedOnRoadmap fw:Roadmap ; backlog:hasRoadmapRank 13 ;
    backlog:scheduledInHorizon backlog:Next ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Source named: the Scrum Guide's sprint planning — the developers select what can be finished within the sprint, against known capacity. hasCapacity and hasEffortEstimate already exist; nothing compares them at commitment time, so an iteration can be committed to more than it can deliver with no objection." .
fw:AC_IterationCapacity a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given an iteration with a declared capacity and stories planned into it, When the suite is run, Then committed effort exceeding capacity is rejected, and an iteration whose deployment carries work it did not plan is rejected." .
fw:S_IterationCapacity a backlog:WSJFScore ;
    backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue 3.75 ;
    backlog:hasUserBusinessValue 5.0 ; backlog:hasTimeCriticality 5.0 ;
    backlog:hasRiskReductionValue 5.0 ; backlog:hasJobSize 4.0 ;
    backlog:scoredAt "2026-08-20T19:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "Time criticality and risk reduction equal and high: an over-committed iteration makes velocity measure something that did not finish, and velocity feeds the forecast, so the error propagates into a claim about the future. Job size larger than grooming because capacity must be compared across a planning event rather than checked on one item." ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .
fw:E_IterationCapacity a backlog:CostEstimate ;
    backlog:hasEffortEstimate 4.0 ; backlog:hasCostBasis "Two constraints over existing capacity and estimate properties" ;
    backlog:estimatedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .

fw:EP_TeamRoles a backlog:Epic ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "BRF-EP14" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "Named team roles as optional vocabulary" ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:startedAt "2026-08-21T09:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:finishedAt "2026-08-21T11:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasActualEffort 2.0 ;
    backlog:hasEvidence fw:Ev_Roles ;
    backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasSupervisionMode backlog:Sup_OnTheLoop ;
    backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-08-21T11:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective fw:Obj_Grounded ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion fw:AC_TeamRoles ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore fw:S_TeamRoles ;
    backlog:hasCostEstimate fw:E_TeamRoles ;
    backlog:rankedOnRoadmap fw:Roadmap ; backlog:hasRoadmapRank 14 ;
    backlog:scheduledInHorizon backlog:Next ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Source named: Satzinger et al. for analyst and design roles, ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119-3 for tester and test manager. TeamRole is deliberately open, so shipping named individuals prescribes nothing and an adopter using none stays conformant — which is why this clears Ex_SingleMethod as well." .
fw:AC_TeamRoles a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the framework's role vocabulary, When a register names a team role, Then each shipped role carries the source it was taken from, and a register naming none remains conformant." .
fw:S_TeamRoles a backlog:WSJFScore ;
    backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue 3.0 ;
    backlog:hasUserBusinessValue 4.0 ; backlog:hasTimeCriticality 2.0 ;
    backlog:hasRiskReductionValue 3.0 ; backlog:hasJobSize 3.0 ;
    backlog:scoredAt "2026-08-20T19:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "Lowest of the three and honestly so: it adds vocabulary an adopter may ignore, and nothing downstream depends on it. Included because the mission requires grounding in standards and these roles are the citable ones the proposal researched." ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .
fw:E_TeamRoles a backlog:CostEstimate ;
    backlog:hasEffortEstimate 2.0 ; backlog:hasCostBasis "Named individuals on an existing open class, each with a source" ;
    backlog:estimatedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .

#################################################################
#  REFUSED BY THE SCOPE — recorded, not built.
#
#  Autonomy-graded evidence: require a Done item produced with
#  Mode_Automated and Sup_None to carry stronger proof than one a
#  person supervised. It closes the third measured gap and this
#  session believes it is right.
#
#  It is not built because Ex_InventedPractice refuses it: no named
#  source relates execution autonomy to the evidence a work item
#  must carry. ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207 and 14764 predate the question;
#  ISO/IEC 42001 governs AI management systems, not work-item
#  evidence. Searching produced nothing citable.
#
#  Recorded as a gap rather than filled with a rule this session
#  reasoned out — which is exactly what the exclusion is for, and
#  the first time this boundary has refused anything.
#################################################################

fw:Gap_AutonomyEvidence a backlog:FitGapFinding ;
    backlog:findingOf fw:Adapt_Register ;
    backlog:findingItem fw:Init_SdlcConcepts ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Third measured gap in Obj_IntentToWork: ExecutionModality records how autonomously work was produced and no constraint relates it to required evidence, so autonomous and non-autonomous work are held to identical proof. No named source exists for the rule, so Ex_InventedPractice refuses it. Raised to the owner as a decision rather than built: either a source is found, or the exclusion is changed deliberately, or the gap stands." .

fw:Ev_Grooming a backlog:TestEvidence ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "03-tooling/fixtures/fixture_grooming_negative_v1_0_0.ttl" ;
    backlog:hasTestId "BRF-EP12" ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-08-20T11:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Five cases exercised on one fixture and each verified individually, not in aggregate. A declares two concerns and addresses both: silent. B addresses one of two: rejected. C declares nothing at all: rejected. D states that none applies with a reason: silent. E declares concerns and simultaneously says none applies: rejected twice. Building it caught a real defect — the first draft matched on backlog:refinedItem, which does not exist; the property is backlog:refines, so the rule would have passed everything while appearing to work." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_validate + pyshacl" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion fw:AC_Grooming .

#################################################################
#  v2.4.0 — BRF-EP15: the technical processes reach the task level.
#
#  The owner asked whether domain engineering, business analysis,
#  technical analysis, design, testing and deployment were part of
#  the framework. Measured: they were not. Only design existed, as
#  five concerns; ExecutionTask carried no properties at all.
#################################################################

fw:EP_TaskTypes a backlog:Epic ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "BRF-EP15" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "A task says which technical process it performs" ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective fw:Obj_IntentToWork ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion fw:AC_TaskTypes ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore fw:S_TaskTypes ;
    backlog:hasCostEstimate fw:E_TaskTypes ;
    backlog:rankedOnRoadmap fw:Roadmap ; backlog:hasRoadmapRank 15 ;
    backlog:scheduledInHorizon backlog:Now ;
    backlog:startedAt "2026-08-20T12:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:finishedAt "2026-08-20T13:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasActualEffort 5.0 ;
    backlog:hasEvidence fw:Ev_TaskTypes ;
    backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasSupervisionMode backlog:Sup_OnTheLoop ;
    backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-08-20T13:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Source named: ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207 clause 6.4, taken WHOLE rather than sampled. The standard's fourteen technical processes are a superset of the six the owner named, and the extras are the interesting part — system analysis, integration and validation are the ones a register loses when it records only what it was asked for." .
fw:AC_TaskTypes a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a story groomed for design concerns and planned into an iteration, When the suite is run, Then every task states which technical process it performs, a concern analysed with no task of the implied type is reported, and a register recording only implementation work is told so." .
fw:S_TaskTypes a backlog:WSJFScore ;
    backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue 6.0 ;
    backlog:hasUserBusinessValue 8.0 ; backlog:hasTimeCriticality 5.0 ;
    backlog:hasRiskReductionValue 5.0 ; backlog:hasJobSize 3.0 ;
    backlog:scoredAt "2026-08-20T12:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "Highest value in the register: it is the layer at which the mission's granularisation actually lands, and without it grooming produced analysis that execution could not be checked against. Job size small because the standard supplies the taxonomy; nothing had to be invented." ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .
fw:E_TaskTypes a backlog:CostEstimate ;
    backlog:hasEffortEstimate 4.0 ; backlog:hasCostBasis "Fourteen individuals from a standard, one property on ExecutionTask, a concern-to-type join, three constraints" ;
    backlog:estimatedAt "2026-08-20T12:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .

fw:Ev_TaskTypes a backlog:TestEvidence ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "03-tooling/fixtures/fixture_tasktype_negative_v1_0_0.ttl" ;
    backlog:hasTestId "BRF-EP15" ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-08-20T13:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Three cases verified individually. A task with no type is rejected at L3. A story groomed for Architecture whose only planned task is Implementation raises the grooming-to-execution advisory. A story groomed for two concerns with tasks of both implied types stays silent. The register-level advisory fires on a backlog holding implementation tasks and neither verification nor validation." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_validate + pyshacl" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion fw:AC_TaskTypes .

#################################################################
#  v2.5.0 — comprehensive fit-gap, and the root cause of the drift.
#
#  Run as a governed LineageAdaptation, all four gates recorded.
#################################################################

fw:Adapt_FitGap a backlog:LineageAdaptation ;
    rdfs:label "Comprehensive fit-gap of the whole register"@en ;
    backlog:adaptsScope fw:Scope_Build ;
    backlog:hasAdaptationStage backlog:Stage_Relink ;
    backlog:hasAdaptationOutcome backlog:Adapt_BoundaryHolds .

fw:Gate_FG_Assess a backlog:AdaptationGate ;
    rdfs:label "Which order was each scope built in?"@en ;
    backlog:gateFor fw:Adapt_FitGap ; backlog:gatesStage backlog:Stage_Assess ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "SELECT ?sc ?m ?fills ?realises WHERE { ?sc a backlog:ScopeStatement . OPTIONAL { ?sc backlog:scopeForMission ?m } }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "one direction per scope" ;
    backlog:hasGateResult "one direction per scope" ;
    backlog:gatePassed true ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Four scopes, each naming its mission, no mixed directions. Three are scope-first; fw:Scope alone is scope-last and is retained as the record of how the original development was built." .

fw:Gate_FG_FitGap a backlog:AdaptationGate ;
    rdfs:label "Does every work item trace to the scope governing it?"@en ;
    backlog:gateFor fw:Adapt_FitGap ; backlog:gatesStage backlog:Stage_FitGap ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "SELECT ?i WHERE { ?i backlog:pursuesObjective ?o . ?o backlog:contributesToGoal ?g . ?g backlog:contributesToMission ?m2 . ?sc backlog:scopeForMission ?m1 . { ?o backlog:fillsScope ?sc } UNION { ?sc backlog:scopeRealizesObjective ?o } FILTER (?m1 != ?m2) }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "enumerated" ;
    backlog:hasGateResult "enumerated" ;
    backlog:gatePassed true ;
    backlog:hasTransitionNote "14 forked chains and 4 untraced execution tasks. Every fork names a SUPERSEDED mission on at least one side." ;
    backlog:hasRationale "The gate passes on having measured, not on the trace being intact." .



fw:Gate_FG_Ruling a backlog:AdaptationGate ;
    rdfs:label "Boundary holds, or must be rewritten?"@en ;
    backlog:gateFor fw:Adapt_FitGap ; backlog:gatesStage backlog:Stage_Ruling ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "ASK { ?f backlog:findingOf fw:Adapt_FitGap }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "owner ruling recorded" ;
    backlog:hasGateResult "owner ruling recorded" ;
    backlog:gatePassed true ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Ruled BoundaryHolds — and the suite caught this session claiming otherwise. The first draft recorded BoundaryRewritten while rewriting no boundary, and the adaptation shape rejected it twice: no new ScopeStatement, no ScopeChange. It was right. Two findings stand and neither is fixed by moving a boundary: the forks are historical and must stay visible, and the self-exemption is a level declaration rather than a scope error. What the ruling changes is the SUITE — the fork rule now exempts superseded lineage, and a new advisory reports a register running below its own target. The owner ruling is on record in this session: 'I am still not feel safe the scope is in the lineage and the lineage is built on this scope.'" .

fw:Gate_FG_Relink a backlog:AdaptationGate ;
    rdfs:label "Carry out what the ruling decided"@en ;
    backlog:gateFor fw:Adapt_FitGap ; backlog:gatesStage backlog:Stage_Relink ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "SELECT (COUNT(*) AS ?forks) WHERE { ?o backlog:fillsScope ?sc ; backlog:contributesToGoal ?g . ?sc backlog:scopeForMission ?m1 . ?g backlog:contributesToMission ?m2 . FILTER (?m1 != ?m2) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s backlog:supersedesMission ?m1 } FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s2 backlog:supersedesMission ?m2 } }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "0" ;
    backlog:hasGateResult "0" ;
    backlog:gatePassed true ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Zero forks in live lineage, verified by test-driving the register at L4. The fourteen historical forks remain in the register and remain visible; what changed is that they no longer block a release, because a superseded mission's chain is a record and not a claim." .

fw:Obs_L3Gap a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "Measured distance to the declared target"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_IntentToWorkGaps ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_IntentToWork ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 1.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-20T15:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Test-driven at all three levels rather than assumed: L2 clean, L3 117 violations, L4 162. The L3 gap is dominated by 48 Done items with no derived test harness and 20 backfilled pre-mission releases that advance no objective — the latter correctly, since they shipped before the objectives existed. Two of the three original gaps are closed by EP12 and EP15; the third, autonomy-graded evidence, remains refused by Ex_InventedPractice for want of a named source." .

#################################################################
#  The two findings, recorded as what they ACTUALLY are.
#
#  FitGapFinding means "work found to fall outside the standing
#  boundary". Neither of these is that — a forked chain is a defect
#  in the intent graph, and a self-exemption is a level
#  declaration. Filing them as fit-gap findings forced the outcome
#  to BoundaryRewritten, and the adaptation shape rejected it: no
#  new scope, no ScopeChange. The shape was right and the filing
#  was wrong.
#
#  The fit-gap found NO work outside the boundary. BoundaryHolds is
#  therefore the correct outcome and rests on a recorded
#  measurement rather than on inspection.
#################################################################

fw:Inv_NoLiveForks a backlog:CrossCuttingInvariant ;
    rdfs:label "No forked chain in live lineage"@en ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "SELECT (COUNT(*) AS ?n) WHERE { ?o backlog:fillsScope ?sc ; backlog:contributesToGoal ?g . ?sc backlog:scopeForMission ?m1 . ?g backlog:contributesToMission ?m2 . FILTER (?m1 != ?m2) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s backlog:supersedesMission ?m1 } }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "0" ;
    backlog:hasInvariantStatus backlog:Holds ;
    backlog:tracksItem fw:Init_SdlcConcepts ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Fourteen forks exist and all name a superseded mission. They are a consequence of missions having been invented one per release batch, each summarising work already done. They stay in the register and stay visible: re-pointing them would assert an intent never held. What changed is that superseded lineage no longer blocks a live release." .

fw:Inv_NoSelfExemption a backlog:CrossCuttingInvariant ;
    backlog:hasInvariantStatus backlog:Holds ;
    rdfs:label "ROOT CAUSE — the register ran below the level its own framework enforces"@en ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "ASK { ?p a backlog:AdoptionProfile ; backlog:hasConformanceLevel ?l ; backlog:hasTargetConformanceLevel ?t . FILTER (?l != ?t) }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "false" ;
    backlog:tracksItem fw:Init_SdlcConcepts ;
    backlog:hasRationale "CLOSED by remediation. This register declared L2 while the framework it publishes enforces at L3 and L4. Test-driven: 16 of 57 level-gated constraints did not run and 166 violations were invisible, including the fourteen forked chains the L4 rule written to catch them could not see. EVERY drift in this package's history has this shape — a rule built at L3 or L4 to prevent a class of error, then never run against the register containing it. Status NotYetEnforceable because closing it needs 48 test harnesses and is real work, not a declaration; the gap is now measured, dated and advised on rather than assumed away." .


#################################################################
#  v3.0.0 — MAJOR. Remediation to L4_LineageEnforced.
#
#  162 violations stood when this register was test-driven at L4
#  while declaring L2. Each is remediated by adding what the
#  constraint asks for, never by weakening the constraint.
#
#  Where a fact is asserted retroactively the rationale says so: a
#  backfilled link with a stated basis is honest, one presented as
#  though it had always been there is not.
#################################################################

#  GROUP 1 — the 20 backfilled pre-mission releases.
#  Earlier releases declined to link these, calling it retrofitted
#  intent. Half right: what they lacked was not intent but a RECORD.
#  They were the initial development and did advance Obj_Derived.
