#################################################################
#  v3.5.0 — the two superseded objectives retired, the missing
#  objective added, and the last gap closed.
#################################################################

#  RETIRED. Obj_Adopter and Obj_Derived measure "can an adopter
#  answer questions without a spreadsheet" — the concern of
#  Mission_Dev, one of the five missions this session drafted and
#  the owner superseded. They are unmet against a purpose the
#  register no longer holds, and they measure the same two
#  refusals twice (cumulative flow, per-dimension cost).
#
#  Retired rather than deleted: they record what was believed and
#  measured at the time. An objective retired with a reason is a
#  decision; one deleted is a disappearance.

fw:Obj_Adopter backlog:hasAchievementStatus backlog:Ach_Withdrawn ;
    backlog:hasRationale "RETIRED at v1.82.0. Measures adopter self-service, the concern of the superseded Mission_Dev. Last observed 2 against a target of 0. Not carried forward: the owner's mission is building software from mission statements, and whether an adopter needs a spreadsheet alongside is not a test of that." .

fw:Obj_Derived backlog:hasAchievementStatus backlog:Ach_Withdrawn ;
    backlog:hasRationale "RETIRED at v1.82.0. The same two refusals as Obj_Adopter expressed as a percentage — 75 of a target 80. Measured a superseded mission and double-counted a single gap." .

#  ADDED. Goal_MissionToWork was measured only by whether the PATH
#  from mission to work is checkable. Nothing measured whether the
#  work that path produced actually COVERS the scope and reached
#  users. That is the owner's test: the deployed package proves the
#  goals are met by physical measure, not by assertion.

fw:Metric_ScopeDelivered a core:Metric ;
    rdfs:label "Share of in-scope work delivered in a package"@en .

fw:Obj_ScopeDelivered a backlog:Objective ;
    rdfs:label "Everything the scope admits is delivered in a package"@en ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:fillsScope fw:Scope_Build ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal fw:Goal_MissionToWork ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric fw:Metric_ScopeDelivered ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetValue 100.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ;
    backlog:hasObjectiveDeadline "2026-12-31T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:metricMovableBy fw:EP_Grooming , fw:EP_TaskTypes , fw:EP_IterationCapacity , fw:EP_TeamRoles , fw:EP_GroundTwo .

fw:Obs_ScopeDelivered a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "In-scope work delivered in a package"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_ScopeDelivered ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_ScopeDelivered ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 100.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-25T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Counted stories that pursue an objective under Scope_Build and checked each against DeploymentUnit membership. Every one is carried by fw:Rel_v1_80_0. This is the physical measure the owner asked for: not that the work is Done, but that it reached users in a package." .

#  Obj_IntentToWork closes: the third gap now has a named source.

fw:Obs_IntentToWorkFinal a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "Steps the suite cannot check — closed"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_IntentToWorkGaps ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_IntentToWork ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-25T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "All three as-is gaps now checkable. Grooming: a story reaching Ready is analysed against every concern it declares. Package sizing: an iteration committing beyond capacity is rejected. Autonomy-graded evidence: work produced with no human in or on the loop must carry evidence attesting a criterion, sourced to ISO/IEC 42001's requirement that oversight be proportionate to autonomy and EU AI Act Art. 14. The source existed and was not looked for hard enough; Ex_InventedPractice correctly held the line for four releases until it was found." .


#################################################################
#  v3.6.0 — the scope gets content of its own.
#
#  The owner observed that the lineage was epic-based: selected
#  epics became the scope and mission subjects. Confirmed, and the
#  mechanism was precise. Obj_ScopeDelivered counted stories
#  pursuing an objective under Scope_Build and divided by the SAME
#  SET — so it read 100%% whether the scope was satisfied or merely
#  emptied, and whatever the epics delivered defined what the scope
#  had wanted.
#
#  The deliverables below are read CLAUSE BY CLAUSE from the
#  owner's mission statement, not from the epics that exist. Each
#  is what must be TRUE, not what someone will do. Work is now
#  measured against them rather than against itself.
#################################################################
fw:Del_Groom a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "Grooming and granularisation: a mission statement is carried down to stories small enough to fit one iteration, and a story reaching Ready has been analysed against every design concern its work touches." .
fw:EP_Grooming backlog:satisfiesDeliverable fw:Del_Groom .
fw:Del_Package a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "Regularly deployable packages: completed work reaches users in a package, and a package records the basis on which its contents were chosen." .
fw:EP_ValueRelease backlog:satisfiesDeliverable fw:Del_Package .
fw:Del_TimeBox a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "Time-boxed iterations planned to finish their package content: an iteration committing beyond its capacity is rejected, and a deployment carrying work its iteration never planned is rejected." .
fw:EP_IterationCapacity backlog:satisfiesDeliverable fw:Del_TimeBox .
fw:Del_Autonomy a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "Execution recorded as autonomous, semi-autonomous or non-autonomous, with the evidence required proportionate to how autonomously the work was produced." .
fw:EP_Human backlog:satisfiesDeliverable fw:Del_Autonomy .
fw:Del_Grounded a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "Practices at each step grounded in a named software engineering standard: no term the framework ships is silent about its provenance." .
fw:EP_GroundTwo backlog:satisfiesDeliverable fw:Del_Grounded .
fw:Del_Granular a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "Work granularised to task level with each task naming which technical process it performs." .
fw:EP_TaskTypes backlog:satisfiesDeliverable fw:Del_Granular .
fw:Del_Checkable a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "Machine-confirmable throughout: every step above is a constraint the suite can check, not a convention a reader is asked to follow." .
fw:EP_TaskTypes backlog:satisfiesDeliverable fw:Del_Checkable .
fw:Scope_Build backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_Groom , fw:Del_Package , fw:Del_TimeBox , fw:Del_Autonomy , fw:Del_Grounded , fw:Del_Granular , fw:Del_Checkable .

#  Obj_ScopeDelivered re-measured against the deliverables rather
#  than against the backlog. The denominator is now what the scope
#  REQUIRES; the earlier figure divided the backlog by itself.

fw:Obs_ScopeDeliveredReal a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "In-scope deliverables satisfied by delivered work"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_ScopeDelivered ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_ScopeDelivered ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 100.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-25T12:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Denominator: the seven deliverables Scope_Build requires, read clause by clause from the owner's mission statement. Numerator: those satisfied by an epic whose stories are carried by a DeploymentUnit. Seven of seven. The previous observation counted stories pursuing an objective under the scope and divided by the same set — both sides were the backlog, so it would have read 100 percent with one story or with none. This figure can fall: adding a deliverable nothing satisfies lowers it immediately, which is what makes the boundary able to refuse." .

#################################################################
#  v3.7.0 — the live lineage staged, with its real history.
#
#  The commits below are read from git, not chosen. They record
#  what actually happened and they are not flattering:
#
#    Mission   a20c9eb   24 Aug 10:53
#    Goal      a20c9eb   24 Aug 10:53   SAME COMMIT as the mission
#    Backlog   79b3a47   24 Aug 11:18
#    Objective 02bc8af   25 Aug 06:28   AFTER the backlog
#    Scope     90c433b   25 Aug 08:24   AFTER everything
#
#  Two findings the pipeline makes visible and nothing previously
#  could:
#
#  1. Mission and Goal closed in the SAME commit, so their order is
#     unwitnessed however it was actually built. The advisory says
#     exactly this.
#
#  2. The scope stage closed LAST. Scope_Build's TEXT was written
#     at a20c9eb, but its DELIVERABLES — the content that makes a
#     boundary able to refuse — arrived at 90c433b, after the epics
#     they were meant to constrain. That is the G17 defect with a
#     commit attached to it.
#
#  Recorded rather than backdated. A stage output naming a commit
#  the author cannot rewrite is worth having precisely when it
#  reports something inconvenient.
#################################################################

fw:Out_Mission a backlog:StageOutput ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Mission ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "6991178527975a2cb68786a1ae250f55c2e258811cfed0cbdd4e6c74c8955bcb" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "a20c9eb" .

fw:Out_Scope a backlog:StageOutput ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "1e1ffa04719f7cdb68dd66c07c85fc38b470b58b85f6e89e69739d0efe9f5e66" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "90c433b" ;
    backlog:consumesOutput fw:Out_Mission .

fw:Out_Goal a backlog:StageOutput ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Goal ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "4916fdbfddb2fcf4f7b511f40f5c4d3857af26f6b2b3d26835c7829e1beb4c21" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "a20c9eb" ;
    backlog:consumesOutput fw:Out_Scope .

fw:Out_Objective a backlog:StageOutput ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Objective ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "12883a89ad0527b7fa32600b77b298cebc8f9f06332cf56a2d99f9af1c5d45aa" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "02bc8af" ;
    backlog:consumesOutput fw:Out_Goal .

fw:Out_Backlog a backlog:StageOutput ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "c4c739d2a56f36e36beff6b4c0791a7573ef718b119b3fd5e5b3a62b806ed7ab" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "79b3a47" ;
    backlog:consumesOutput fw:Out_Objective .

#################################################################
#  v3.8.0 — SCOPE STAGE ONLY. No epics in this commit.
#
#  The owner asked whether analysis and design artefacts — UML and
#  traditional models, diagrams, specifications, interaction steps,
#  state changes, test cases and test data — are part of the
#  framework. Measured: they are NOT. The phase taxonomy is fixed
#  (14 ISO 12207 task types, 5 design concerns) and every modelling
#  and test-specification concept is absent.
#
#  Under the v5.0.0 staged ceremony this commit closes the SCOPE
#  stage and nothing else. The deliverables below say what must be
#  true; the epics that satisfy them are written in a LATER commit,
#  so the boundary provably precedes the work rather than being
#  drawn around it.
#
#  This is the first time this package has separated those two
#  commits. Every previous scope had its deliverables arrive after
#  the epics — the defect ScopeContentLateShape reports on
#  Scope_Build to this day.
#################################################################

fw:Del_Model a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "A story's analysis and design work produces named model artefacts, and the framework can say which kind each is — structure or behaviour — using a taxonomy taken from a modelling standard rather than invented." .

fw:Del_Spec a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "A story carries a specification of what it does: the interaction steps a user performs, and the state changes those steps cause. A story whose behaviour is described only in prose cannot be checked against what was built." .

fw:Del_TestSpec a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "An acceptance criterion is exercised by named test cases with named test data, so evidence points at a specific check rather than at a claim that testing happened." .

fw:Scope_Build backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_Model , fw:Del_Spec , fw:Del_TestSpec .

fw:Metric_ModellingGaps a core:Metric ;
    rdfs:label "Analysis and design concepts the framework cannot express"@en .

fw:Obj_Modelling a backlog:Objective ;
    rdfs:label "Analysis, design and test specification are expressible"@en ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:fillsScope fw:Scope_Build ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal fw:Goal_MissionToWork ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric fw:Metric_ModellingGaps ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue 8.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease ;
    backlog:hasObjectiveDeadline "2026-12-31T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Obs_ModellingAsIs a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "As-is: modelling and test-specification concepts absent"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_ModellingGaps ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_Modelling ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 8.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-25T14:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Enumerated against the shipped TBox by direct class lookup, not by recollection. ABSENT: ModelArtifact, Diagram, UseCase, Specification, TestCase, TestData, StateChange, InteractionStep — eight. PRESENT and correctly fixed: TaskType with 14 ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207 technical processes, DesignConcern with 5 Satzinger design activities, AcceptanceCriterion, DefinitionOfDone, TestEvidence, TestHarness. So the PHASES are fixed on both grooming and task-type creation, as the owner asked; what is missing is everything those phases PRODUCE. A task can say it performed design definition and cannot say what design it produced." .

fw:Obs_ScopeDeliveredAfterWidening a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "In-scope deliverables satisfied — after the boundary widened"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_ScopeDelivered ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_ScopeDelivered ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 70.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-25T14:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "7 of 10 deliverables satisfied. The figure FELL from 100 percent, and that is the point: three deliverables were added and nothing satisfies them yet. Under the old metric — which counted stories pursuing an objective and divided by the same set — this would still have read 100 percent, because the denominator was the backlog. A coverage figure that cannot fall is not measuring a boundary, and this one just did." .


#################################################################
#  v3.9.0 — BACKLOG STAGE. The scope closed at commit ceb950d.
#
#  Three epics, one per deliverable, written in a LATER commit than
#  the boundary they answer to. That separation is the whole point
#  of the v5.0.0 ceremony and this is its first real use: every
#  earlier scope in this register had its deliverables arrive after
#  its epics.
#
#  Each epic names the standard its work will be grounded in,
#  before the work starts, because Ex_InventedPractice requires it.
#################################################################

