#  Roadmap, Commitment_Dev, DoD and Scope are referenced by the
#  shared Register and by live work, so they are framework-wide
#  rather than lineage-scoped — found when the archive split left
#  them pointed at from both sides. The Lineage individuals
#  themselves are framework-wide too: they ARE the index, and an
#  index that archives with its contents cannot be searched.

#################################################################
#  The archive split is BLOCKED, and the blocker is named.
#
#  With every individual carrying belongsToLineage, the split was
#  attempted: 805 retired individuals, 7063 archive triples, 68
#  percent of the register. Then the live side was checked for
#  edges pointing into the archive, and seven remain:
#
#    scopeForMission, scopeRealizesObjective, hasScopeExclusion
#    roadmapRealises, commitsToGoal, hasDoDCriterion
#    lineageForMission
#
#  Every one comes from a SHARED CONTAINER. There is one Register,
#  one Roadmap, one Scope, one Commitment, one DefinitionOfDone,
#  and all seven lineages hang off them. The containers cannot go
#  to the archive because live work uses them, and they cannot stay
#  whole because they reference retired work.
#
#  lineageForMission is the exception and is CORRECT: the Lineage
#  individuals are the index, they stay live, and an index pointing
#  at what it indexes is what an index is for.
#
#  So the modelling gap has two halves and this release closes one.
#  belongsToLineage exists, is carried by 1147 individuals, and is
#  enforced at L2 — an unassigned work item is now a violation and
#  the 297-constraint failure cannot recur. The second half is
#  PER-LINEAGE CONTAINERS, and it is a separate piece of work
#  rather than something to force through here.
#################################################################

fw:Obs_ArchiveBlocked a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "Archive split, and what blocks it"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_Obj_CodeDecisions ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_CodeDecisions ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-27T17:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Measured with membership in place: 805 retired individuals, 7063 archive triples, 68 percent of the register, and seven edge types still crossing from live into the archive. All seven originate at a shared container — one Register, one Roadmap, one Scope, one Commitment, one DefinitionOfDone serving seven lineages. Not loading the archive was measured earlier at 139.5s to 79.8s, a 43 percent saving, so the prize is real and the blocker is structural rather than a matter of effort." .

fw:Inv_PerLineageContainer a backlog:CrossCuttingInvariant ;
    rdfs:label "A container serves one lineage"@en ;
    backlog:hasCheckQuery "ASK { ?c backlog:hasScopeStatement|backlog:roadmapRealises|backlog:commitsToGoal ?x . ?x backlog:belongsToLineage ?l1 . ?c backlog:belongsToLineage ?l2 . FILTER (?l1 != ?l2) }" ;
    backlog:hasExpectedResult "false" ;

    backlog:tracksItem fw:EP_ScriptDecisions ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Violated: five shared containers serve all seven lineages, and each is referenced by live and retired work at once. Recorded rather than worked around, because forcing the split by cutting those edges would produce exactly the corruption this release exists to prevent — a live register pointing at individuals that are no longer there." .

#  Gate K caught two defects in one header. The v7.12.0 bump never
#  landed — the block still read 7.11.0, so the 8.0.0 replacement
#  matched nothing and silently did nothing, while the FILENAME
#  moved to 8.0.0 and the changelog announced it. Two releases were
#  described as versions the file did not claim.
#
#  And owl:priorVersion carried TWO values on a functional
#  property, from a bump whose replacement also missed. A chain of
#  versions that forks is not a chain.
#
#  Both found by a gate whose whole job is comparing three
#  statements of the same number — the kind of check that looks
#  redundant until the day the three disagree.

#################################################################
#  v8.1.0 — the mission statement, read back, settles the floor.
#
#  The owner asked me to read the mission statements rather than
#  the counters. Mission_OntologyDriven says:
#
#    "What remains as prose EXPLAINS; what remains as code executes
#     standard engines. NEITHER CARRIES MEANING THAT ONLY THEY
#     DEFINE."
#
#  Obj_RowsUnchecked counts rows whose first cell does not resolve
#  to a TBox term. That is a PROXY for the mission clause and not
#  the clause itself, and the proxy and the clause disagree on the
#  last fifteen rows.
#
#  Tested one by one against the actual clause — is this row's
#  meaning defined anywhere but the prose?
#
#    the fit-gap gate passes on measured        AdaptationGate, gatePassed
#    a gate whose result contradicts            the gatePassed clause
#    digests catch fabrication                  StageOutput, hasStateDigest
#    digests miss backwards construction        closedAtCommit
#    order needs an external witness            closedAtCommit
#    the witness has a measured limit           hasDurationSource
#    the facing rows                            GoalFacing
#    the five artefact-file rows                ArtifactEvidence, Manifest
#    every item traces to an objective          pursuesObjective + L4 clause
#    every epic decomposes                      decomposesInto, EpicSpecifiedShape
#    no item pursues an out-of-scope objective  fillsScope + clause
#
#  ELEVEN of eleven. Every remaining row EXPLAINS something the
#  ontology already defines and enforces. Not one carries meaning
#  that only it defines.
#
#  So the objective is MET on its mission's terms and its counter
#  reads 15 on a proxy that was never the requirement. Recorded as
#  Ach_Retrospective — the count stays at 15 permanently rather
#  than being adjusted, because adjusting it would be the exact
#  fabrication this framework exists to catch.
#################################################################

fw:Obj_RowsUnchecked backlog:hasAchievementStatus backlog:Ach_Retrospective ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Retrospective, and the reason is the mission clause rather than the count. Obj_RowsUnchecked counts rows whose first cell resolves to a TBox term, which is a PROXY for the requirement that prose carry no meaning only it defines. Each of the fifteen remaining rows was read against the real clause and each explains something the ontology already defines and enforces — AdaptationGate and gatePassed, StageOutput and hasStateDigest, closedAtCommit, hasDurationSource, GoalFacing, ArtifactEvidence, pursuesObjective, decomposesInto, fillsScope. Eleven of eleven. The count stays at 15 permanently; adjusting it so the objective could read 0 would be the fabrication this framework exists to catch." .

fw:Ev_MissionRead a backlog:TestEvidence ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "04-documentation standard table rows against Mission_OntologyDriven" ;
    backlog:hasTestId "rows-vs-mission" ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-08-27T18:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Each of the fifteen rows resolved individually against the TBox and shapes to find where its meaning is defined. Eleven distinct claims, eleven found enforced. The one that looked unenforced — a gate marked passed whose observed result contradicts its expectation — is carried by the gatePassed clause comparing hasExpectedResult to hasGateResult, found by reading the clause rather than grepping its message." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "manual resolution against tbox and shapes" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion fw:AC_EP_StandardRows_S2 .

fw:Mission_OntologyDriven backlog:hasMissionOutcome backlog:Out_Achieved ;
    backlog:outcomeRationale "Achieved. Six objectives met outright: governance rulings queryable 18 to 0, classification tables exported 23 to 0, scripts deciding what is valid 3 to 0, rules decided in code 3 to 0, and the two containment ceilings held at 0. The seventh, Obj_RowsUnchecked, carries Ach_Retrospective: its counter reads 15 on a proxy for the mission clause, and each of the fifteen rows was read against the clause itself and found to explain something the ontology already defines and enforces. Every goal is reached or has a status saying why it no longer steers, which is the only condition under which this outcome may be set." ;
    backlog:retiredAtCommit "pending-commit" .

fw:L_OntologyDriven backlog:lineageArchived false .

#################################################################
#  v8.2.0 — every container states its scope.
#
#  Assigned by reading MEMBERSHIP, not by naming: a container whose
#  members all belong to one lineage is lineage-scoped; one whose
#  members span lineages, or which has none, is framework-scoped.
#  Computed rather than listed, because the last hand-written
#  classification in this package was wrong six times out of six.
#################################################################

