#  Roadmap, Scope, DoD and Commitment_Dev are not subclasses of
#  WorkItemContainer, so the membership walk never reached them —
#  the walk was right and its starting point was too narrow. Each
#  is scoped here by the lineage of what it POINTS AT, which is
#  how the others were done.
fw:Roadmap backlog:containerScope backlog:CScope_Framework .
fw:Scope backlog:containerScope backlog:CScope_Framework .
fw:DoD backlog:containerScope backlog:CScope_Lineage ;
    backlog:containerForLineage fw:L_Dev .
fw:Commitment_Dev backlog:containerScope backlog:CScope_Lineage ;
    backlog:containerForLineage fw:L_Dev .

#################################################################
#  The residual, measured and named.
#
#  Roadmap references six lineages and Scope three. Those are not
#  misclassifications — a roadmap that RANKS work across lineages
#  genuinely spans them, and ranking across lineages is what a
#  roadmap is for. They stay framework-scoped and stay live.
#
#  DoD and Commitment_Dev reference L_Dev alone and are scoped to
#  it, so they archive with it.
#
#  What remains after container scoping: 14 live-to-archive edges
#  from two genuinely cross-lineage containers, down from the
#  original 7 edge types across 5 containers. lineageForMission is
#  among them and is CORRECT — the Lineage individuals are the
#  index and an index points at what it indexes.
#
#  So the archive can be built with Roadmap and Scope retaining
#  pointers into it. That is a reference to an archived item, not a
#  dangling one, and the difference is whether the archive file
#  exists and is named — which archiveFile now requires.
#################################################################

fw:Obs_ContainerScoped a backlog:MetricObservation ;
    rdfs:label "Container scoping, and what still spans lineages"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_Obj_CodeDecisions ;
    backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_CodeDecisions ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 0.0 ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-08-27T19:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Thirty-three containers scoped by reading what their members and references belong to, not by naming them: 31 lineage-scoped, 2 framework-scoped. Four were missed on the first pass because they are not subclasses of WorkItemContainer and the membership walk started there — the walk was right and its starting point too narrow. Roadmap spans six lineages and Scope three; both are genuinely cross-lineage and stay live. Residual live-to-archive edges: 14, from two containers, down from 7 edge types across 5." .

fw:Inv_PerLineageContainer backlog:hasInvariantStatus backlog:Holds ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Holds with a stated exception. Every container now declares its scope, and 31 of 33 serve exactly one lineage and archive with it. Roadmap and Scope span lineages by their nature — ranking and boundary-setting across runs is what they do — so they stay live and retain named pointers into the archive. A pointer into a named archive file is a reference, not a dangling edge, which is why archiveFile is required of an archived lineage." .
